 Paragraph 2:
   - Defines dominance: a tuple ti dominates tj if for every attribute ti[k] >= tj[k] and at least one attribute ti[k] > tj[k].
   - Gives an example (in Example 1) of dominance: t1 dominates t2.
   - Defines the skyline (Pareto-optimal set) as the set of tuples that are not dominated.
   - Introduces the concept of a "maxima representative" (a subset S of D that contains the maximum for any ranking function).
   - States that the skyline is the minimal representative for monotonic ranking functions and the convex-hull for linear ranking functions.
   - Points out that the skyline (or convex-hull) may be too large (80% of the dataset in Example 1) and thus not practical for decision making.

